WEBVTT

00:00:14.170 --> 00:00:17.740
<i>Nishifujinomiya. Nishifujinomiya.</i>

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.240
I'm at Fujinomiya

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.710
<i>This is way closer than Kofu.</i>

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:25.500
Okay!

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:27.180
Off I go!

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.260
Fujinomiya's known for yakisoba, right?

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.180
I can't wait!

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.250
This is Cape Ohmama.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.890
What a nice view of Mt. Fuji!

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:13.480
This is the kiritanpo 
hot pot we had together.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.440
It turned out nice, didn't it?

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:20.240
Kiritanpo is like something in between 
fried rice balls and fried rice cakes, huh?

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.450
Wait, never mind that photo...

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:28.430
And this is Iida-san and her dad, 
who saved us from the freezing cold.

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.660
Toba-sensei's there, too!

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.250
Rin told Sensei what was going on.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.470
If she hadn't, who knows
 what would've happened?

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:37.450
Same with me!

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.340
Rin-chan saved me at Lake Motosu, too.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:45.640
We're gonna have to call her "Shimarin-sama"
 out of gratitude and reverence!

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.390
You're right, Ena-chan!

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:53.490
Great Shimarin-sama, 
please accept our offering.

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:55.670
Praise be. Praise be.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:56.750
No worshiping.

00:02:57.320 --> 00:03:05.660
<b>(2) Episode 7 
Nadeshiko's Solo Camp Planning</b>

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:02.450
Wait, do you not have Outclub today?

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.660
The others have to work, so we're not meeting.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:10.590
I haven't been able to do anything with 
the club since I started work, either.

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:12.700
I kind of miss it.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:14.080
I see...

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:15.890
Hey, Ena-chan!

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:18.660
Why don't the three of us hold
 an emergency Outclub meeting?

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.660
Hey, good idea, Nadeshiko-chan.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:22.430
I never gave you permission to include me.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.900
Then again, I have somewhere 
to be today myself.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.640
See you.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:36.110
By the way, Nadeshiko, are you 
serious about going solo camping?

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.040
Yeah.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.300
I'm thinking of going this week 
since I have time off work.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.730
Why, though?

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:42.450
Remember?

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:48.740
You said solo camping is a totally different 
experience from camping with other people.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.190
That made me want to try it, too.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:59.250
So I figured I'd ask you
 all about solo camping!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.900
<i>I never realized I was encouraging her.</i>

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.550
How do you usually pick a place to camp?

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:11.050
I search for "campsites" on 
Glueglue Maps to find a few spots,

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:14.710
then do some research to 
find out more about them.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:18.480
Campsites

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:18.480
Oh, yeah, it might be easier 
to find a place on Maps.

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:22.160
It's also a good idea to 
check out campers' blogs.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.710
They talk about things you wouldn't 
know unless you went there.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:27.540
Oh, this place seems nice.

00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:30.610
Look, the view is great.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:31.990
Oh, here?

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.130
It's way up in the mountains, though.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.750
It might be too hard to walk up.

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.570
Wait, aren't you getting 
a ride from Sakura-san?

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.490
Nah.

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:43.560
Since I'm solo camping, I'm thinking 
of going on foot from the train or bus.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:49.880
Besides, I'm pretty sure if I told her
I'm going camping alone, she'd say no.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.160
<i>By yourself?!</i>

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.960
What are you going to tell 
her when you leave, then?

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.770
I-I think I'll tell her 
I'm going with my friends.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.220
You're so lucky, Rin-chan.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.300
You get to go anywhere 
you want on your moped.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.280
Maybe I should get a license, too...

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:06.710
<i>She'd fall over.</i>

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:08.710
<i>She'd get stranded without gas.</i>

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.900
<i>She'd take the wrong route and get lost.</i>

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.540
Your face says no...

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:15.480
So, is there anything else to keep in mind?

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:17.040
Let me think...

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.540
Shimarin's
<b>Camping Course</b>

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.360
<i>Shimarin's Camping Course.</i>

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:24.960
<i>One: choose a campsite that's 
within cellular range.</i>

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.940
Choose a campsite that's 
within cellular range

