Decorative Book

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:10.140
Decorative Book

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:10.640
Decorative Book

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:16.480
Decorative Book

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:13.390
What I'm going to do?

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.720
You'll get bored if you go 
solo camping without plans.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.990
<i>Start a fire, have a meal...</i>

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:21.640
<i>The end.</i>

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:22.790
That's what happens.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.000
What to do, huh?

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.510
It can be anything.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.110
You can knit or take a 
walk around the campsite.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:36.260
Sake, sake...

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:37.610
Found it.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:40.120
<b>Ikeike</b>

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:40.120
This is the one I had in Iida-san's tent.

00:06:42.530 --> 00:06:45.630
<i>That sake was so good, and it 
paired so well with the hot pot.</i>

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.880
I heard what happened, Toba-sensei.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:51.970
That you went to Lake Yamanaka 
to pick up Ohgaki and the others.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.770
Good thing nothing bad happened, huh?

00:06:54.770 --> 00:06:56.880
Yes, it really is.

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:59.350
Hey, that's Ikeike.

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.890
You know of it?

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:06.210
A local sake shop recommended it to me when 
I went to Izu with my hiking club last year.

00:07:06.210 --> 00:07:08.000
Izu's great, isn't it?

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:10.000
It has plenty of mountains and water...

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:10.900
Hey, that's it.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:15.530
Why don't you take the club to 
Izu for their winter camping?

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:21.000
They could camp there safely without 
worrying too much about the cold.

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:23.540
Izu, huh?

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:28.050
<i>Please be sure to stop by 
our shop if you're ever in Itou.</i>

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.890
<i>It might be nice to go.
 I do owe them, after all.</i>

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:33.800
Izu Highland Cherry Blossom St.
<b>Iida Liquors</b>

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.220
Thanks, Rin-chan!

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.680
I have a pretty good idea how 
to start solo camping now.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:39.780
All right!

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:43.690
I'm going to get my research in before the
 weekend and make my solo camper debut!

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.150
Well, I should head home.

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.460
Oh, okay.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:50.830
See you tomorrow!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.350
<i>Nadeshiko's going weekend solo camping, huh?</i>

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:07.120
<i>Yeesh.</i>

00:08:13.810 --> 00:08:17.900
<i>I have the weekend off work too, actually.</i>

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:24.480
You're going camping by yourself, you say?

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:30.010
I-I know it's winter, but it's warmer 
than here, and it's not too far.

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:33.960
Be sure to stay safe.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:35.510
What? Really?

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:36.990
